azarg","html_url":"https://github.com/elazarg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-09-05T18:41:26Z","updated_at":"2016-09-05T18:41:26Z","body":"I believe that this is a result of the special casing of both `Enum` and `NamedTuple`. It can be special-cased too at [subtypes.py](https://github.com/python/mypy/blob/master/mypy/subtypes.py#L122-L123):\n\n```\n        right = self.right\n+       if isinstance(right, TupleType) and right.fallback.type.is_enum:\n+           return is_subtype(left, right.fallback)\n        if isinstance(right, Instance):\n```\n\nI think that this special casing is justified, but I'm not sure.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/244797626/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"elazarg","id":5108069,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMDgwNjk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5108069?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg","html_url":"https://github.com/elazarg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/elazarg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/use